IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), piece cb5 -- THE NOUNS THE MODULES OF PARTS XIX TO XXI SHARE.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. The text this was encoded from is a plain-text rendering of the Department of Justice
-- Canada consolidation current to 2026-09-30 (last amended 2026-03-26); it is not an official version,
-- and nothing here has been verified against the official text. Contains information licensed under
-- the Open Government Licence - Canada.
--
-- WHAT THIS MODULE IS. Types only, no rule of the Act. The shared vocabulary of the whole Act is in
-- cbca-core.l4 (the keel); this module holds only what two or more modules of piece cb5 need and the
-- keel lacks. Every name here is specific to what it decides, because the names of all pieces end up
-- in one folder.

§ `Nouns shared by the modules of piece cb5`

§§ `A maximum punishment on summary conviction -- s 235(4), s 235(5), s 250(1), s 250(2)`

-- The Act states a ceiling, never a tariff: "a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars or ...
-- imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to both". The sentence actually passed is a fact
-- about a case that the court decides; the record below holds only the most the court may impose.
-- src:2924 | (4) A person who fails to comply with this section is guilty of an offence and liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to both.
-- src:3118 | is guilty of an offence and liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to both.
@ref CBCA s 235(4), s 250(1) (src:2924 src:3118)
DECLARE `Maximum punishment on summary conviction` HAS
    `largest fine in dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `longest imprisonment in months` IS A NUMBER
    `fine and imprisonment may both be imposed` IS A BOOLEAN
